#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2240 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "H2 guard scenario (WORKORDER-H2-guard-coverage / REVIEW1B-date-order-flip.tsv): subject 001 HAS DS records but every DSSTDTC cell is blank, so max_date over the group yields EmptyResult.MISSING and the not empty($max_ds_dsstdtc) guard silences the rule despite a populated LBENDTC. If this FIRES, the order-flip guard was deleted: post-6c totality makes date(--ENDTC) > MISSING true on every dated row."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#library dataset-class LB FINDINGS
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBENDTC  type=Char label="End Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | ALT | 2020-01-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | MOVED TO RECOVERY   | RECOVERY            |
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE  | TERMINAL SACRIFICE  |
